<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user}>
  <.chrome here="Privacy&amp;Policy"></.chrome>

  <div class="pbody">
    <.section title="What cab stores" pad>
      <p>
        <b>Accounts:</b> your username, display name and e-mail as provided by the
        sign-in provider (GitHub today). We never see your password.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Participation:</b> session signups, room draws, ballots and the scores
        judges submit. Standings and personal stats are computed from exactly these
        records and nothing else.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Guests:</b> registering through a shared link stores the name you enter
        and a personal access link scoped to that one session. The club head can
        revoke it at any time.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="What cab does not do" pad>
      <p>
        No analytics trackers, no advertising, no sale or transfer of data to third
        parties. The only cookie is the session cookie that keeps you signed in.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Your requests" pad>
      <p>
        Export, correction or deletion of your data — write to
        <a href="mailto:support@uadebate.com">support@uadebate.com</a>
        and we will answer within 30 days. Deleting an account anonymises your name
        in past results instead of silently rewriting club history.
      </p>
      <p class="mut">
        cab is in beta testing; this policy grows with the platform. Operated by the
        NGO Debate Federation of Ukraine (ВМГО «Федерація Дебатів України»).
      </p>
    </.section>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
